# SendTrajectory.action — DRY action surface.  Core schema is embedded
# (TrajectoryGoal → TrajectoryResult), not mirrored by hand.  Feedback keeps
# the classic per-step fields (state / step_progression / error) that the
# execution feedback timeline carries (§5: "feedback: unchanged").
TrajectoryGoal goal              # start_pose + goalsets (planner context; never re-planned)

# MTC parity (ExecuteTaskSolution): MTC drives each SubTrajectory's stored
# RobotTrajectory VERBATIM — it never re-derives the plan, so there is no cache
# to miss and no IK branch to jump. The caller fills this from the validated
# plan it already holds (the trajectory it was shown), and the server stages +
# streams it as-is; `goal` is then only a hint (the planner still comes from
# SetPlanner). There is NO cache-reuse / re-solve execute path: an open-loop
# execution with no trajectory is an error, not a silent re-plan. Reactive
# (MPC/retarget) planners ignore `replay` and servo live instead.
bool replay
trajectory_msgs/JointTrajectory replay_trajectory
---
TrajectoryResult result          # success / message / trajectory / stats / collisions
---
# Feedback — status carried ONLY by the action feedback (no status topic).
string state              # PLANNING | EXECUTING | TRACKING | ON_TARGET | FAILED
float32 step_progression  # open-loop progress [0..1]
float64 position_error    # current Cartesian error (m), reactive
float64 position_error_x  # signed per-axis component of position_error (m)
float64 position_error_y
float64 position_error_z
bool on_target            # reactive servoing flag
sensor_msgs/JointState joint_command
float64 orientation_error # rad between tool and goal orientation, FK-measured
int32 hold_count          # consecutive in-tolerance steps below convergence threshold
float64 controller_position_error     # instantaneous (controller's own estimate)
float64 controller_orientation_error
